  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Acrylic glass inlays",
   "anchor": "intarzie"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "An inlay is an illuminated panel with protruding or recessed characters.",
   "anchor": "intarzie"
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Graphics: the better choice for small signs set in very fine typefaces, which could not be shaped as a standalone 3D sign.",
   "anchor": "intarzie"
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Material: the body is formed by an aluminium frame and back panel. The front face is covered with an opaque board, usually sheet metal or a sandwich board – Dibond.",
   "anchor": "intarzie"
  },
  {
   "type": "li",
   "text": "Placement: an advantage on historic buildings, for example, where drilling into the façade is not possible – the power supply runs to a single point only.",
   "anchor": "intarzie"
  },
  {
   "type": "a",
   "text": "Request a no-obligation quote",
